# 7. COMPLETE FRONTEND FIREBASE AUTH

This is now P0.

The browser must use Firebase Authentication.

Implement/configure the Firebase Web SDK.

The frontend needs:

```text
initializeApp()
getAuth()
```

and appropriate authentication flows.

Support:

```text
signup
login
logout
auth-state restoration
password reset
email verification if used
```

Use:

```javascript
onAuthStateChanged(...)
```

or the appropriate current Firebase mechanism for restoring auth state.

Do not continue relying on:

```text
express-session
__session
/api/auth/session backed by PostgreSQL
```

---

# 8. AUTHENTICATED FUNCTIONS REQUESTS

Where frontend requests privileged API operations through Functions:

obtain the Firebase ID token.

Concept:

```javascript
const token = await user.getIdToken();
```

Send:

```http
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

The Functions authentication middleware must verify:

```javascript
admin.auth().verifyIdToken(token)
```

Use the verified:

```text
uid
```

for ownership.

Never trust a frontend-provided UID.

---

# 9. AUTH BOOT SEQUENCE

Rewrite application initialization carefully.

Desired behavior:

```text
load page
↓
initialize Firebase
↓
initialize Firebase Auth
↓
wait for initial auth state
↓
authenticated
    → load application
unauthenticated
    → show login/register
error
    → show recovery UI
```

The previous blank-screen failure must never return.

There must always be:

```text
loading state
authenticated UI
login UI
or error UI
```

Never an unexplained blank page.

---

# 10. FIREBASE WEB CONFIG

Use the correct Firebase Web configuration for the existing project.

Remember:

Firebase Web config values such as:

```text
apiKey
authDomain
projectId
storageBucket
messagingSenderId
appId
```

are identifiers/configuration rather than server-side secrets.

However:

Do not put:

```text
Firebase Admin private keys
service-account JSON
payment secrets
SMTP secrets
M-Pesa secrets
```

in frontend JavaScript.

